# Testing Rules

## Framework

- PHPUnit 11 for backend
- `tests/TestCase.php` as base class (extends Laravel TestCase)
- Feature tests in `tests/Feature/`, Unit tests in `tests/Unit/`
- `phpunit.xml` config with SQLite in-memory for tests

## Test Conventions

- Test file names match pattern: `{Feature}Test.php`
- Use `RefreshDatabase` trait in feature tests
- Use model factories for test data
- Test both authorized and unauthorized access flows
- Test validation rules explicitly

## Key Test Patterns

```php
// Feature test
class BoardTest extends TestCase
{
    use RefreshDatabase;

    public function test_user_can_create_board(): void
    {
        $user = User::factory()->create();
        $workspace = Workspace::factory()->create();
        // ... assert responses, redirects, DB state
    }
}
```

## What to Test

- All policy methods (viewAny, view, create, update, delete)
- Controller CRUD operations
- Validation rules reject invalid data
- Authorization denies unauthorized users
- Soft deletes work correctly
- Slug generation is unique
- UUID generation on model creation
